						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Not as a single built-in switch. Message Streams gives transactional and broadcast email separate sender reputation so a marketing-list bounce doesn't poison your password-reset deliverability. Vectis Mail routes all outbound through one Postfix queue, so you set up that separation yourself — running separate Vectis Mail installs (one for transactional, one for broadcast) or using different sending domains with separate DKIM keys. It's configuration work rather than a one-click feature, and worth scoping up front if multi-stream reputation separation is core to how you send." }
