						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "What about deliverability on a self-hosted server?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "On a fresh VPS IP you build reputation rather than inherit it: plan for 2–4 weeks of gradual IP warmup before a new IP reaches an equivalent standing. You don't take a day-one hit when migrating — the dual-send playbook keeps your current provider delivering production mail while your Vectis Mail IP warms, so there's no reputation gap during the switch. After warmup, self-hosted deliverability with DKIM/SPF/DMARC/MTA-STS properly configured comes down to your IP reputation and DNS hygiene, and Vectis Mail ships those configured correctly by default." }
					}
				]
			}
